is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I could not reproduce the reported outage between Office A and Office B. From the affected client (pc1, 10.1.0.100), end-to-end IP and application connectivity to the campus server (srv1, 10.5.0.4) is healthy. Evidence:
- ICMP from pc1 to 10.5.0.4: 0% loss, ~2 ms RTT (ttl=61), confirming L3 reachability across the inter-office path.
- HTTP from pc1 to http://10.5.0.4: completes in ~1.6–1.8 ms total time on repeated tests, confirming successful TCP sessions and application responsiveness.
- Topology-wide checks show hosts in Office A (pc1, pc2) and Office B (pc3) can mutually reach each other with 0% loss, indicating the core and distribution layers are up.

Mechanism: If the “link between buildings” were down, ICMP and TCP to 10.5.0.4 would fail or show high loss/latency; neither is observed. Routing and switching planes appear stable, and the server responds promptly.

Localization: Verified directly on endpoints pc1 (10.1.0.100) and srv1 (10.5.0.4). No anomalies detected on the interconnecting path.

Root cause: No current network fault; the issue was likely transient during/after the maintenance window or unrelated to the inter-site link (e.g., endpoint/application/DNS hiccup).

Corrective fix: No network changes required. Advise the user to retry and, if the problem recurs, capture exact timestamps, application/port details, and error messages so we can correlate with logs. We will continue to monitor, but at present the Office A–Office B connection is operational. 
